      "flagged": [],
      "note": "Repeated invocations are counted MECHANICALLY: the identical tool and identical arguments, by digest. A repeat is not a finding that the work was wasted -- polling until a condition holds, retrying a flaky step, and re-reading a file that changed all repeat legitimately, and this instrument cannot tell those from a stuck loop because that needs the state the transcript does not record. What it gives you is where to look. Matching is EXACT, which under-reports on purpose: a retry whose arguments differ by a timestamp or a page token does not match, and no normalisation is shipped because none of the obvious ones is grounded -- the same reason no threshold is shipped. So treat a count here as a floor."
